          "text": "The local three is r160 and npm has `three@0.160.0`? npm three versions: 0.160.0 exists. And `3d-tiles-renderer@0.3.34` is on npm. So I'll use:\n- `three@0.160.0` (exact match to vendored lib that the prototype was verified against)\n- `3d-tiles-renderer@0.3.34` (matches local package)\n\nDRACO decoder files: copy from `libs/draco/` into `public/draco/` — the prototype used `./libs/draco/`. I'll vendor those 3 files (1MB) into the app's public dir for offline reliability.\n\nWait, does the npm three 0.160 include examples/jsm/libs/draco? It does, but vendoring our verified copy is safer. Actually let me just copy the same libs/draco files we already have — they're verified working with the local three.module.js DRACOLoader. But npm three's DRACOLoader version might differ slightly in wrapper API expectations. To be safe, use DRACO imports from npm three examples too:\n`import { DRACOLoader } from 'three/examples/jsm/loaders/DRACOLoader.js'` and setDecoderPath('draco/') with vendored files. The draco decoder wasm is version-agnostic. The three DRACOLoader expects draco_decoder.js? It detects wasm support. Vendored files are the standard ones from three examples. Should be compatible.\n\nHmm, actually simpler and fully verified: DRACOLoader.setDecoderConfig? That requires importing decoder files as modules. setDecoderPath + static files in public/ is simplest. Copy from our libs/draco (they came from three examples, standard).\n\nNow the repo layout. Current kph2026-07:\n- README.md (tracked, CraftStadium template)\n- app/ (untracked, Cesium nagashi-somen Vite app) — package.json name is odd, has node_modules\n- nagashi-somen/ (untracked)\n\nPlan: create new files at repo ROOT:\n- package.json, package-lock.json (npm install will generate)\n- vite.config.ts, tsconfig.json\n- index.html\n- src/*.ts\n- public/draco/* (3 files)\n- README.md → fill in template\n- Move app/ → legacy/nagashi-somen-app/ (untracked, so moving is safe — no git impact) to avoid two package.json/vite projects colliding with root dev/build detection. Actually app/ has node_modules (huge) — moving it would move node_modules too. Moving is a rename, cheap. Let me move `app` to `legacy/nagashi-somen-slider`... Hmm, but the dist/ inside app/ is the current CraftStadium deployed build maybe? If CraftStadium currently deploys from app/, moving it might break the current deploy (they may want to keep it until the new one is verified). Since I can't verify CraftStadium's config, I'll keep app/ in place and just add root-level app. Then when I'm ready, push and let the user decide. Actually two vite projects in one repo could confuse deploy (root build works with root package.json). CraftStadium likely does `npm install && npm run build` at root of the pushed repo — root package.json will define the game. That's the standard.\n\nDecision: keep app/ untouched for now; build root-level app. At the end, mention to the user they can delete app/ once deploy confirmed.\n\nNow — game design details. Let me write down the spec (since user delegated):\n\n**作品名**: 「KAGINAWA ― 忍者、京都の空を翔る」 (Ninja Kaginawa: Kyoto Sky Run)\n\n**コンセプト**: PLATEAU 京都市の実在のビル群 (三条〜四条烏丸〜京都駅) を、鉤爪(カギナワ)による振り子移動で疾走する3Dスイングアクション。観光地「にぎわい」創出テーマ。\n\n**ゲーム性** (Time Attack + Score):\n1. スタート: 四条烏丸交差点上空のビル塔上\n2. ゴール: 京都駅 (本当の京都駅ビルの位置)\n3. コース上に 鳥居ゲート (torii) × 5 (四条烏丸 → 烏丸御池 → 四条大宮? → 七条? → 京都駅) — real coordinates along the corridor. Passing through gives checkpoint + time bonus.\n4. 小判 (koban coins) floating along likely swing paths — collect for score.\n5. スコア = 小判×100 + 最高速度ボーナス + 未接地コンボ + ゴールタイム逆数ボーナス。Best time & score to localStorage.\n6. 失敗: 地上/街中に墜ちると数秒ロス and respawn slightly above; no game over.\n7. リザルト画面: タイム, スコア, ベスト更新表示, もう一度ボタン.\n\n**技術**:\n- Vite + TypeScript + Three.js r160 + 3D-Tiles-Renderer 0.3.34\n- PLATEAU 2025 京都市 LOD2 (下京区・中京区) 3D Tiles / B3DM (Draco) — CMS assets から直接取得 (CORS OK)\n- 地理座標: ECEF + ENUローカルフレーム (WGS84)\n- 物理: カスタム振り子 (ロープ拘束 + ポンプ加速 + リリース boost)\n- エフェクト: 速度連動FOV・speed vignette・風パーティクル・画面シェイク\n- 音: WebAudio 合成 (風・鉤爪・小判・ゴールDJ・和風BGM)\n- モバイルタッチ対応\n\n**コース座標** (四条烏丸〜京都駅, real world):\n- 四条烏丸: lat 34.9945? Hmm: 四条烏丸交差点 ≈ 35.0033, 135.7598? Let me recall Kyoto geography. 京都駅: 34.9858, 135.7588. 四条烏丸: 35.0034, 135.7598. Distance ~2km N-S. The prototype's spawn: 34.9965,135.7585 at 130m. ORIGIN: 34.994, 135.758.\n\nCheckpoints (all along 烏丸通 ≈ lon 135.7595, going south from 四条 to 京都駅):\n1. 四条烏丸 (35.0034, 135.7598) — start at ~80m\n2. 烏丸御池? Actually 御池通: 35.0067? No wait. Shijo-Karasuma 35.0034/135.7598. 御池通 is north of 四条 (35.0067). Going south: 四条 (35.0034), 五条 (34.9958?), 七条 (34.9910?), 八条 (34.9886), 九条 (34.9862), 京都駅 (34.9858).\n   - Ring 1: 烏丸姉小路? Let me just do: 四条 (start), 五条烏丸 (34.9958), 七条烏丸 (34.9910), 八条烏丸 (34.9886), 京都駅 (34.9858, 135.7588) = goal.\n   - Heights ~100-140m (above rooftops, below building tops at 40-70m... Kyoto buildings LOD2 around 20-40m, station building taller). Rings at 80-140m work for swinging.\n\nCoins: place along corridor between rings at swinging heights (90-160m).\n\nAlso add decorative: 烏丸通 street-level neon like prototype, 京都駅前の大階段? Keep prototype FX.\n\n**Implementation file layout** (kph2026-07 root):\n- index.html (game UI: loading, title card, HUD, result)\n- src/main.ts — game orchestrator\n- src/geo.ts — WGS84→ECEF, ENU basis, spawn/course coords\n- src/plateau.ts — tiles + fallback city\n- src/street.ts — neon/lamps/cars/wind (from prototype)\n- src/ninja.ts — hero rig + poses\n- src/player.ts — swing physics\n- src/course.ts — rings/coins/checkpoints\n- src/audio.ts — WebAudio synth\n- src/hud.ts — HUD DOM\n- public/draco/* — decoder\n- README.md\n\nThat's a fair amount but doable. Let me be pragmatic: keep the prototype's proven code, refactor into modules, add game layer.\n\nLet me start scaffolding. First npm init at root and install deps. Note: root dir has a package.json? No. Create fresh.\n\nActually — the root dir name has Japanese chars and a space: \"1010　Hackathon\" (with full-width space!). kph2026-07 is inside. Fine.\n\nOne more consideration: the prototype uses `import * as THREE from 'three'` mapped to local libs. With npm, `three` resolves to node_modules/three/build/three.module.js and `three/examples/jsm/...` to node_modules/three/examples/jsm/... Good. `3d-tiles-renderer` → node_modules/3d-tiles-renderer/src/index.js. Let me check the local index.js exports to confirm TilesRenderer export name (\"3d-tiles-renderer/three\" was aliased to same file — the 0.3.34 package has a single index.js with all exports).",
