          "text": "Installed. Now verify the exports resolve and check the TilesRenderer API in the npm version matches what the prototype used.\n\nNow write the game. Design files:\n\n1. `index.html` — UI shell (loading, title, HUD, result), styles\n2. `src/geo.ts` — WGS84→ECEF + ENU basis helper + course coordinates\n3. `src/config.ts` — constants (tileset URLs, course data, tunables)\n4. `src/audio.ts` — WebAudio synth\n5. `src/plateau.ts` — tiles renderer + fallback city + street dressing (neon, lamps, cars, stars, moon, wind)\n6. `src/ninja.ts` — hero mesh + pose\n7. `src/player.ts` — swing physics + rope visual + input\n8. `src/course.ts` — torii rings + koban coins + checkpoint logic\n9. `src/hud.ts` — HUD updates + result screen\n10. `src/main.ts` — orchestrator: scene, camera, loop, game state machine (title→playing→result)\n\nLet me carefully design the physics/gameplay to be actually fun and robust:\n\n**Coordinate system**: ECEF world like the prototype. UP = normalized origin. east/north tangential basis at ORIGIN. All entities positioned via ORIGIN + east*A + north*B + up*H. Local \"map\" coords (A=east km?, B=north). For gameplay logic, I'll work in a local ENU frame with units in meters, and convert to ECEF for rendering. Actually simpler: keep prototype approach (ECEF vectors) but implement helper `place(vec, east, north, up)`.\n\nActually cleaner: define a local coordinate frame: all game positions in \"world-local\" meters: x=east, y=up, z=-north (so that it looks like standard three.js Y-up in local space, with north = -z). Then a single root Object3D holds everything, with its matrix converting local→ECEF. But 3D-Tiles-Renderer needs camera in world (ECEF) coords; TilesRenderer adds its group to scene (ECEF). Mixing local frame objects and ECEF tiles requires converting camera matrix: set the root Group's matrix to the ECEF transform, and set `camera.matrixWorld` in ECEF? TilesRenderer.setCamera(camera) uses camera.matrixWorld presumably; if camera is child of a rotated group it still works because matrixWorld is composed in world space. Scene graph with root group at ECEF transform works: camera MatrixWorld = local compose * group matrixWorld = ECEF. So I can:\n\n- scene (ECEF)\n  - envGroup (Object3D) with matrix set from basis (east/north/up at ORIGIN) + position ORIGIN → local coords\n    - hero, rope, rings, coins, street props, fallback city\n  - tiles group (ECEF, tiles renderer output)\n  - stars, moon (positioned in ECEF directly)\n\nCamera: needs to be in scene root? If camera is child of envGroup, then camera.matrixWorld is correct ECEF; TilesRenderer uses camera matrices; raycaster against tiles group uses world coords too. Camera position/matrixWorld auto-updates if matrixAutoUpdate default. The prototype sets camera.position directly (ECEF) with no parent. With the group approach, camera.parent = scene, position ECEF — but then converting player local→ECEF each frame. Both work.\n\nSimplest and least error-prone: **do everything in ECEF with helper basis vectors** (like the prototype). No group transforms. Just always use helper: `v.copy(ORIGIN).addScaledVector(EAST, x).addScaledVector(NORTH_UNIT, z).addScaledVector(UP, y)`.\n\nI'll define course data in geographic coordinates (lon/lat/height) and convert.\n\n**Player physics** (from prototype, tuned):\n- gravity 26 (units m/s²? it's game-y), MAX_ROPE 260\n- attach: raycast from camera center; if hit within 260m and above player → attach at hit point\n- rope constraint: position clamp + radial velocity removal + pump\n- release: vel *= 1.6 + up*12\n- auto-shoot: when falling and no attach, try shoot forward-up after interval\n- reel in on hold\n\n**Course**: \n- Start tower: on a building near 四条烏丸? Simpler: spawn in air at (四条烏丸, 140m) with initial forward velocity.\n- 5 torii gates + goal torii (bigger, red) at 京都駅.\n- Coins: arcs between consecutive gates.\n- Checkpoint logic: when player passes through ring plane within radius (e.g. 18m of ring center), activate: +score, time bonus, flash, chime, set next target. Arrow indicator points to next ring.\n- Fall below ~30m over street → reset to above last checkpoint (auto), small penalty time (2s?). Actually \"接地ドジ\" — simply respawn at checkpoint.\n\n**Scoring**: koban 100 each; checkpoint 1000; combo multiplier per air-time; speed record; final score; time recorded. Best in localStorage.\n\n**HUD**: speed km/h (big), altitude, timer, koban count, combo, next-target arrow + distance, top best time.\n\n**Result screen**: time, score, new record?, restart button (R also restarts).\n\n**Audio** (WebAudio synth):\n- wind: brown/white noise through lowpass, gain by speed\n- whoosh on release: noise burst with bandpass sweep\n- thunk attach: short filtered noise + low sine thump\n- coin: bright pentatonic chime (sine 1046→1568)\n- checkpoint: koto-ish pluck (two-tone)\n- goal: fanfare arpeggio (pentatonic)\n- fall: descending saw\n- BGM: simple generative koto+penta loop with reverb-ish delay (hackathon-friendly, no assets)\n- All created on first user gesture (start button) to satisfy autoplay policy.\n\n**Ninja look**: prototype's rig is fine — red 忍者 suit (0x7d0d1d), dark mask, white eyes, scarf? Add a scarf/布 trailing: a strip of quads following head (simplify: a line of small planes with feedback positions). Add a kaginawa grapple: the rope line + anchor ball exist; add claw mesh at anchor (small cone cluster)? Keep ropeLine + anchorBall + add claw.\n\n**FX**: \n- speed vignette (CSS) ✓\n- wind particles ✓\n- FOV ✓ (62→100)\n- screen shake ✓\n- attachment impact: ring pulse at anchor (scale-fading torus)\n- coin sparkle: point flash\n- checkpoint: expanding ring + text\n- speed lines (CSS radial streak) ✓ from prototype\n- motion blur skip (postprocessing Pass exists but keep simple)\n\n**Street FX**: keep prototype's neon/lamps/cars/stars/moon/night-day toggle, placed along 烏丸通 corridor (real world coords, along north-south through the course). Also maybe add 京都駅ビルの highlight? Not necessary.\n\n**Rings placement** (geographic, along 烏丸通 from 四条 to 京都駅):\n- CP1 四条烏丸: 35.0034, 135.7598, alt 150 (ring just above 四条交差点)\n- CP2 五条烏丸: 34.9958, 135.7592? Let me verify: 五条通 lat ≈ 34.9958 (五条大橋?). 五条烏丸 ≈ 34.9956, 135.7588.\n- CP3 七条烏丸: 34.9910, 135.7585? 七条通 lat ≈ 34.9908.\n- CP4 八条烏丸: 34.9886, 135.7584? 八条通 ≈ 34.9887.\n- GOAL 京都駅: 34.9858, 135.7588, at 120m above station (station building ~60m tall; tower 130m... Kyoto Station tower is 130m; place ring at ~150m above ground so you pass above the tower).\n\nActually let me double check these are roughly right (0.006 lat ≈ 660m). 四条烏丸 (35.0033) → 京都駅 (34.9858) = 0.0175° ≈ 1.94km. Good.\n\nI should verify actual lat/lon via the PLATEAU API or GSI quickly? These are well-known: 京都駅 34.9858, 135.7588 is right. 四条烏丸 35.0033, 135.7598 close. 五条烏丸 34.9955. 七条烏丸 34.9912? 七条通 ≈ 34.9909. 八条烏丸 ≈ 34.9886. Fine — approximate is OK (rings are in the air, gameplay tolerances).\n\nCoins between at swing heights (~90-170m).\n\nDistance ~1.9km; a good swing run at ~40-60 m/s takes 40-60s. \n\n**Auto-assist grapple** is essential for fun: raycast center, if nothing, try forward+up cone samples.\n\n**Performance**: tiles at LOD2 for 2 wards; raycast against tiles each frame is heavy — prototype does raycast on shoot only + autoTimer 0.4s. Fine.\n\n**Code size**: This will be ~1500-2000 lines total. Let me write it carefully but efficiently. I'll write modules one by one.\n\nLet me also confirm how `TilesRenderer` in npm 0.3.34 is imported: `import { TilesRenderer } from '3d-tiles-renderer'` — from index.js at package root. \n\nTypeScript: 3d-tiles-renderer ships .d.ts alongside .js in src/. Does package include types mapping? \"main\": \"src/index.js\", and there's src/index.d.ts — TS with moduleResolution \"bundler\"/\"node\" will look for src/index.d.ts. Good. three has types included.\n\ntsconfig for vite: standard vite tsconfig with strict maybe false for speed. I'll set strict: true but