          "type": "reasoning",
          "text": "Now main.ts — the orchestrator. Responsibilities:\n\n1. Renderer, scene, camera setup (ECEF scene + env group via LocalFrame.applyToObject)\n2. Create City, Street, Course, Ninja, Player, Hud, GameAudio\n3. Loading flow: probe tilesets → createTiles → when first load-model (or probe complete/fallback), hide loading, show title\n4. Start game: hide title, show hud, audio init + music start, pointer lock, reset player, start timer\n5. Game loop: tiles update, player update, course update, street update, wind, combo/timer logic, HUD update\n6. Game events: checkpoint (banner, score, respawn point), coins, fall, goal → result screen with score + best time (localStorage), retry, day/night toggle\n7. Resize\n\nCombo logic: combo increments while airborne; resets on fall/checkpoint? Let's define: combo = number of grapple swings since last ground/air reset? Simpler: combo counts \"連続アタッチ\" without touching ground & without falling: each attach +1 combo multiplier (max x9); falling resets to 0. Coins score = coin.value * combo? Let's do score = sum over coins (100 * combo at pickup time) + 1000 per checkpoint + speed bonus... Actually simpler and readable:\n- score = coins*100 + checkpoints*1000 + max(0, 15000 - time*50)... hmm confusing. Let me do:\n  - score = coins * 100 * (1 + combo)?? Overcomplicating.\n\nFinal scoring:\n- Each koban: 100 pts × current combo multiplier (combo = number of successful swings since last respawn/attach-chain without touching ground; each swing attach +1). Actually combo increments on each new attach, resets on fall.\n- Checkpoint: 2000 pts\n- Goal bonus: max(0, round(20000 - finalTimeMs/10))? Let me: goal bonus = 1000 + max(0, 600 - elapsed seconds * 10) * 10. Hmm.\n\nSimple: goal bonus = max(1000, 20000 - floor(elapsed * 100)); time bonus displays.\nTotal = coins + checkpoints + goal bonus. Best time in localStorage; record if time < best.\n\nHUD \"BEST\" shows best time formatted.\n\nTimer: starts when start pressed; stops at goal. Falls: +3s penalty (PHYS.fallPenalty).\n\nCourse.update returns hitGate + coinCount. On hitGate i:\n- if goal: finish(): audio goal, result screen, save best.\n- else: banner \"◯◯を制覇! +2000\", audio.checkpoint, score += 2000, player.setCheckpoint(gateCenter).\n\nWind: street.updateWind(dt, player.pos, player.vel, fwd, playing && speed>8). fwd = player.viewDir(new Vector3).\n\nNight: initial night=true. street.setNight(true, scene) at init.\n\nLoading progress: not linear; I'll fake progress: after tiles create, progress = min(1, buildingsLoaded/60); when fallback-only (probe failed / 10s), force complete. Simpler: show title when (first load-model) OR (probe done && liveTilesets===0) OR 10s timeout. Also loading card hides and title shows.\n\nCamera initial: place for a cinematic orbit around Kyoto Station area before start? Nice: while title is shown, camera orbits slowly around the corridor center (四条烏丸〜京都駅). Implement preview orbit: camera position rotates around center point (500m up). Let me add: if state==='title': cinematic orbit; else player.update drives camera.\n\nAlso during 'loading'/'title', still update tiles (so buildings stream in) and street.\n\nPlayer.setPlaying(true) on start; also during title, player physics not updated (player hidden? ninja group visible at spawn — during title cinematic the ninja sits at spawn point; fine, give him a 'fall' pose).\n\nReticle: only when playing.\n\nLet me also handle visibility change (pause?) — skip.\n\nPointer lock: request on start and on canvas click. On pointer lock exit, keep playing (mouse look stops) — fine.\n\nOne important detail: `env.applyToObject` sets matrixAutoUpdate=false and matrix makeBasis — but child objects with matrixAutoUpdate default true compute their own local matrices; three composes parent.matrix * child.matrix when parent.matrixWorld is updated. For env (matrixAutoUpdate=false, matrix set, matrixWorldNeedsUpdate must be set!). If matrixAutoUpdate=false and matrix changed, need `env.matrixWorldNeedsUpdate = true` after setting matrix. Let me handle: in LocalFrame.applyToObject, after setting matrix/position, set `obj.matrixWorldNeedsUpdate = true` and also `obj.matrixWorldAutoUpdate`... Actually Object3D.updateMatrixWorld: if matrixAutoUpdate → updateMatrix(); if matrixWorldNeedsUpdate || force... `this.matrixWorldNeedsUpdate || force` then multiply. Setting `matrixWorldNeedsUpdate = true` once is enough (it's reset in updateMatrixWorld). Good.\n\nAlso stars are in env (local frame) — radius 60000 local — fine.\n\nGround in city.group (child of env) — rotation.x=-PI/2 → local horizontal plane. Good.\n\nSun position in street.group (env child) — DirectionalLight target added to group ✓.\n\nTiles: city.group added to env? NO — tiles must be in the ECEF scene (their coordinates are ECEF). In City I add tiles groups to this.group, and city.group is added to env by main. That's WRONG — tiles would be transformed by env matrix (offset/rotated) while their internal matrices are ECEF-based. Must add tiles directly to scene (ECEF). Fix: City takes two parents: `envGroup` for fallback/ground (local), and adds tiles to `scene` (ECEF).\n\nLet me fix city.ts: constructor(frame, camera, renderer, statusCb, scene) — add tiles groups to scene. The raycaster targets are world-space anyway.\n\nAlso `ground` + `fallback` are local → city.group goes into env. City.group should then be added to env; tiles separate into scene. I'll store `this.tilesGroupParent = scene`.\n\nUpdate city.ts accordingly.",
